---
description: Next.js App Router conventions for apps/web
globs: apps/web/app/**,apps/web/components/**,apps/web/next.config.ts
alwaysApply: false
---
- This Next version differs from your training data. Read the relevant guide in `apps/web/node_modules/next/dist/docs/` before writing code.
- App Router only. Server Components by default; add "use client" only for state, events or browser APIs.
- Route handlers are thin: parse input, call a function from `@dekko/core` or a Convex function, return JSON.
- `params` in route handlers is a Promise; await it.
- No secrets in client components. Only NEXT_PUBLIC_ variables reach the browser.
- Import shared logic from `@dekko/core` (already in `transpilePackages`). Do not copy it into the app.
- Minimal UI: one primary action per screen. Follow the four-step brief in docs/SPEC-F1.md.
